    "rationale": "Elevated IGF-1 despite severe prenatal and postnatal growth failure indicates resistance at the IGF-1 receptor rather than failure to synthesize ligand. Pathogenic IGF1R variants reduce receptor activation/autophosphorylation and downstream signaling in target tissues. Strongest alternative resolved: Growth-hormone receptor defects cause low IGF-1 despite high GH; this patient has markedly elevated IGF-1, a pathogenic IGF1R variant, and reduced fibroblast response to IGF-1, establishing receptor-level IGF-1 resistance."
